Follow-up after the full run: added `enabling_concurrent_heartbeat_after_construction_has_no_executor` to prove the pinned Java boundary when the live enable flag is turned on after construction did not create an executor. The focused loopback test passed. Test-only commit `7e0992d`; strict all-target Clippy, formatting, diff, comparator, and manifest checks are rerun with the documentation commit.

Route DTO input boundary continuation (2026-10-08 21:17 UTC): extended `RuntimeRouteFixtures.routeDtoInputCases` from 25 to 37 actual Java inputs. Twelve new syntax/shape cases show that route `JSON.parseObject` rejects single quotes, comments, unquoted keys, trailing commas, `L`/`D`/`F` numeric suffixes, scalar filter-list values, array-shaped maps, scalar route rows, and null map values. These establish a strict route DTO parser boundary distinct from the separately audited permissive SOCKS constructor parser. Rust's native route DTO decoder rejects the same inputs. Fixture SHA-256 `6de3936438f326e57114da010a1363ae730c7a17de2913293472c7c91547c6bf`; Java oracle/native test commit `aa34861`.

Validation: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol route_dto_inputs_match_invoked_java_fastjson --locked` passed; `mvn -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` completed BUILD SUCCESS, including route/config/heartbeat replay and manifest22; `cargo fmt --all --check` and `git diff --check` passed. No production parser behavior changed. Updated ADR-0014, API map, requirement audit, runtime inventory, Java compatibility summary, and this append-only log. Wider DTO/input/source/field/branch reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

VIP address helper source correction (2026-10-08 21:23 UTC): pinned `MixAll.brokerVIPChannel` uses `lastIndexOf(':')`, parses the suffix with Java `Integer.parseInt`, subtracts two with signed i32 wrap, and preserves the host without validating it. The existing native helper had added a u16/host validation gate. Added 15 actual Java edge cases (empty host, negative/out-of-range ports, i32 boundaries/overflow, plus sign, whitespace, Unicode decimal digits, malformed strings, IPv6-like host, and disabled identity) plus native comparison. Oracle/test commit `7a44d14`; focused regression failed before the fix on `:10911`.

Rust now reuses `java_number::parse_long`, checks Java i32 bounds, and uses `wrapping_sub(2)`; the lower remoting connection owns socket validation. Implementation commit `1850bb6`. Focused `vip_` unit tests pass (3 cases); full workspace/all-target tests pass with test-owned loopback; strict all-target/all-feature Clippy passes; offline Maven verify completes BUILD SUCCESS with route/config/heartbeat fixture replay and manifest22; comparator self-test, fmt and diff checks pass. The first sandboxed filtered run was denied its loopback socket; authorized focused and full reruns passed. No Broker was contacted. Current route fixture SHA-256 `ce2afec05859a761ce2fd82a9034ef147b333f077a999b03d17209a305254fb0`. Updated route audit, API map, requirement audit, runtime inventory, ADR-0014 fixture pointer, Java compatibility summary, and this log in the documentation commit. Broader source/API/field/branch reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.

VIP error-branch mapping continuation (2026-10-08 21:26 UTC): Java no-colon input raises `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException`; bad, blank, whitespace, and out-of-range integer suffixes raise `NumberFormatException`. Rust now maps those source branches to `RuntimeError::InvalidBrokerAddress` and `RuntimeError::InvalidBrokerPort` respectively, and the Java fixture differential asserts the distinct variants. Implementation follow-up commit `e7e6422`. Full workspace/all-target tests and strict all-target/all-feature Clippy pass after the typed error change; the focused VIP differential passes. Documentation now records typed branch mapping and retains the JVM exception-name boundary. Final Maven, formatter, comparator, and diff gates are rerun with the documentation commit.

Route DTO inherited serialization update (2026-10-08 22:03 UTC): pinned Java 5.5.1 source confirms `TopicRouteData` and `TopicQueueMappingInfo` inherit Fastjson2-backed `RemotingSerializable` methods. Added six direct cases for default, explicit-null, and populated instances of each DTO; cases invoke compact/pretty JSON, instance/static encoding, decode, list decode, and fromJson. Fixture hash `935426217262daeb92860ef9b90cc61b5cde8aa71d3042ca6f4713582568e2b3`. Oracle commit `c8bb22a`.

Rust adapters `java_to_json/java_encode/java_decode/java_decode_list/java_from_json` reproduce tested sorted property output, unquoted numeric `brokerAddrs`/`currIdMap` keys, tabs and empty pretty containers. Route API response decoding now uses `TopicRouteData::java_decode`; a scripted loopback RPC consumes actual Java encoded bytes. Implementation commit `4a271dd`. Java map iteration is unspecified, so native map output is deterministic and only invoked case ordering is compared.

