SOCKS Fastjson escape update (2026-10-08 22:11 UTC): extended `RuntimeConfigFixtures.socksConstruction` with actual Java construction/reflection cases for malformed `\x`/`\u` digits, escaped quote forms, line continuations, and a trailing backslash. Java accepts complete-width escapes and maps each invalid ASCII hex digit to zero (`\xG0`→U+0000, `\xG1`→U+0001, `\u12G4`→U+1204); truncated escapes and line continuations reject. Oracle commits `1a8ae75` and `3432e6a`; 126-case fixture SHA-256 `2457d9c7c181805b46c9ae0ca848e1357f3a652f235be56e9f3d82ef834ccde0`.

The existing Rust constructor/reflected-field differential first failed on accepted `\xG0`. `1e54b61` normalizes complete-width Unicode/hex escapes to valid JSON escapes, retaining the U+FFFD boundary for isolated surrogates. The 126-case focused differential now passes.

